/obj/item/paper{
	default_raw_text = "The Northstar-class is equipped with an engine waste temperature control system as standard.<br>To set it up, follow these steps:<br> 1. Wrench in the plasma can.<br> 2. Turn on the waste cooling gas pump and set the thermomachines to the desired temperature (if you're not sure, set them to cold).<br> 3. Set the scrubbers in the chamber to Siphoning in the air alarm.<br> 4. Turn on the filter to the canisters as desired, or replace it.<br> 5. Turn on the Engine Waste to Atmos pump.<br> 6. Inside atmospherics, turn on the Engine Waste to Filter pump, or use the waste however else is desired.<br>Once everything on that list is complete, make sure the gas isn't building up inside the chamber or pipes and you're done.";
